    <text>
        <body>
            <div type="edition" subtype="primary" xml:space="preserve" xml:lang="grc" resp="#VM #JP" source="#autopsy">
                <ab>
                    <lb n="1"/><persName type="divine"><name><hi rend="ligature">Ἄρ</hi>κος</name></persName>
                </ab>
            </div>
            <div type="apparatus">
                <listApp>
                    <app>
                        <note>Text from autopsy</note>
                    </app>
                </listApp>
            </div>
            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#JP">
                <p>Arkos</p>
            </div>
            <div type="commentary">
                <p>Manganaro suggested that the text referred to Arkos, a personification of 'security' (the word also means 'bear', and occurs as a personal name). Orsi speculated on [Συ]ρακοσ[ιος] or [Ἱε]ρακος, but neither of these seems plausible, given that the ligature should render ΑΡ, not ΡΑ, and there would seem to be a vacat before the Α. The letter forms perhaps suggest a third century BCE date, given the combination of broken bar alpha and open sigma.</p>
            </div>
